  "invariants": [
    "Budget approval never grants OBSERVE, EXPERIMENT, MODIFY or ACT authority.",
    "The USD 10/day paid model/API ceiling remains finite, reservation-gated, provider-gated, idempotent and kill-switch controlled.",
    "Ordinary GitHub workflow starts and runner minutes are workload, not paid model/API budget, and never consume the USD ceiling.",
    "Every non-deterministic model/API execution requires a durable reservation immediately before provider invocation.",
    "A paid reservation overage activates a preflight hard stop for subsequent paid model/API execution on the same UTC day.",
    "GitHub workload controls use bounded timeouts, per-service concurrency/event coalescing, duplicate suppression in the owning subsystem and service-specific schedule rates instead of daily start quotas.",
    "Essential reporting and health publication are independent from paid-spend admission and remain able to explain a paid block.",
    "Paid model/API workflows share portfolio-paid-cost-ledger so artifact-backed financial accounting cannot race.",
    "Non-paid workflows use service-specific concurrency groups so unrelated pending jobs cannot replace one another.",
    "Idempotency keys suppress duplicate paid spend and collisions fail closed.",
    "Retry groups cannot reset attempt numbers to bypass paid retry ceilings.",
    "Actual token and cost usage is committed against the reservation; a paid overage triggers a hard stop.",
    "Kill switches may stop paid execution without granting or widening action authority.",
    "Only sanitized IDs, hashes, numeric usage and evidence references may be persisted while BLK-005 is open."
  ],
